The residual shows that the six rules do not preempt another evaluator; they
are the language's missing evaluation contexts for Test inside #choose.

For adversarial completeness, the reviewer also tried to prove the six
contextual reductions after removing those contexts:
  kprove /audit-output/evidence/context-bridge-connection-spec.k
    --definition semantic-no-bridge-kompiled
    -I /tmp/audit-work/80-is-happy/no-bridge
    --spec-module AUDIT-CONTEXT-BRIDGE-CONNECTIONS
Exit: 1
The first residual remains #choose(#short3(eps), ...), as expected for the
deliberately incomplete no-context semantics. This is not a candidate positive
proof failure. Static review of the actual context rules shows four exhaustive
and disjoint PString-shape cases and two exhaustive/disjoint Int equality cases;
each right-hand side is exactly the branch selected by the corresponding
#short3 or #same equation.
